# Project README

## Overview
This project is based on a Figma design that you should duplicate into your own Drafts to access all layers, components, and detailed specifications. Make sure to install the required fonts and follow the interaction notes below to accurately implement the design.

## Figma Access
- Create a Figma account if you don’t have one.
- Open the provided project link.
- Click **“Duplicate to your Drafts”** to get full access.
- If you cannot access the project directly, use the provided `.fig` file and import it into Figma.

## Required Fonts
The design uses custom fonts. Install them before coding:
- **Source Sans Pro**
- **Spin Cycle OT**

If the fonts are not installed on your device, you may download and install them manually before starting development.

## Development Notes
### Responsive Behavior
Your implementation must switch to the **mobile version** when the screen width is **480px or less**.

### Hover & Active States
- **Links:** `#FF6565`
- **Buttons:** `opacity: 0.9`

### Layout Constraints
- Maximum content width: **1000px**, centered on the page.

## File Structure (Recommended)
```
project-folder/
│── index.html
│── styles.css
│── script.js
│── assets/
│   ├── images/
│   └── fonts/
└── README.md
```

## How to Use This README
- Follow each section as a checklist while building the project.
- Use the Figma design as the single source of truth.
- Match spacing, colors, typography, and breakpoints as closely as possible.

